# 18. Buyer Blind Matching

The ideal architecture is a blind marketplace.

Buyer asks:

> Find users satisfying X.

IntentBank responds:

> 18,492 potentially qualifying users.

The buyer does not initially know their identities.

IntentBank distributes the offer.

Only users who accept progress into the next permission state.

This prevents buyers from browsing consumer profiles.

